==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[One Horn]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 96% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 1~6 seconds<sup>30f~180f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 3~8 seconds<sup>90f~240f</sup>.
**3 [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 0.07~0.13 seconds<sup>2f~4f</sup>.
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The main threats of this stage are the four One Horns that spawn when the base is hit. Due to the One Horns' high damage, [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] such as [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] will die very quickly. Effective counters to these are good [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] crowd-controllers, such as [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] and [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]], assuming you have them.

Another viable strategy is to simply out-DPS the One Horns and kill them before they become a threat. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] is great at this, as he can one-shot all of the One Horns at level 20. If you do not yet own Bahamut, [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] also works alongside the [[Cat Cannon]] to provide good damage while keeping the One Horns at bay. Midrange units like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] can quickly stack up damage while staying a safe distance from the One Horns. Any anti-Red [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Super Rares]] will prove to be quite effective here.

